1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ===Om Dyste===
2 CONT Owners of the original Dyste-farm 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1528: Tord paa Düste.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1557: Jonn Dyste.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1612: Berte.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1616: Erik.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1636-1675: Nils Andersen Dyste (1591-1676). He was the son of Anders Dyste (1565-).
2 CONT
2 CONT 1675-1678: Nils Nilsen Dyste (1649-1678), married to Marte Pedersdatter Skjefstad (and with her our bloodline starts at the Dyste-farm).
2 CONT
2 CONT 1678-1680: Nils’ widow, Marte Pedersdatter Dyste (born Skjefstad), married Svend Pedersen Hägär (1649-1715).
2 CONT
2 CONT Svend Pedersen Hägär took the name Dyste. He owned the original Dyste-farm in 1680-1710. In 1710 he sold one half of the farm to Bent Evensen Bay  (1677-1765). Bent´s part was called ”Nistua”. The other half, called ”Oppistua”, Sv
2 CONC end kept on running for another five years, until 1715. Then his son, Christian Svendsen Dyste (1695-1772), took over the farm.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bent Evensen Bay was born at Riise, Hof, Østre Toten, Oppland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bent run the farm “Nistua” from 1710 to 1746. He married Dorte Michelsdatter Rustad (1682-1760) and got eight children with her. Kirsti was the oldest and Kari was the youngest of his children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kirsti married Christian Svendsen Dyste (1695-1772), son of the man who owned the original unsplit Dyste-farm, Svend Pedersen Dyste (1649-1715). She then became the leading lady of the farm ”Oppistua”. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The farm ”Nistua” was passed over to Kari Bentsdatter Dyste and her husbands. Kari´s first husband, Peder Paulsen, ran ”Nistua” from 1746, until he died in 1752. Her second husband, Gulbrand Anderssen Rogneby (1722-1808), run the 
2 CONC farm during the years 1752-1786, until he passed it over to his son, Anders Guldbrandsen Dyste (1758-1833). 
2 CONT
2 CONT This means that after the first split of the Dyste-farm, both parts was joined together again into our bloodline on both sides by Kirsti Bentsdatter´s marrige to Christian Svendsens Dyste. Later on these two parts of the Dyste-far
2 CONC m was also split in two, making the original Dyste-farm into four different farms today.
2 CONT
2 CONT ”Dyste” was one of Totens big farms and many people travelled through even before Holy Olav´s time. The Dyste church was built in the 1100-1200 century and made the farm a stop for pilgrims on their way to Nidaros in Trondheim. On
2 CONC  the 3rd of april 1396, Asbörg Haraldsdatter gave away part of the farm to the Mariachurch in Christiania (Oslo). The church was torn down in the 1780´s, because it was in really bad shape. A well preserved altarstone on the lot o
2 CONC f  the Dyste-farm called "Oppistuen" is the last remains of the church. Five wooden figures of saints, a wooden painting and a few more smaller things remains in the Oldsaks-collection. One wooden statue of a saint is kept at ”Opp
2 CONC istuen”, one of four farms after the original Dyste-farm have been split. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gamle brev og dokumenter hvor Dystegården blir nevnt med ulike skrivemåter:
2 CONT
2 CONT Brev datert den 6. Januar 1349, Aas:
2 CONT
2 CONT Tre Mænd kundgjöre, at Björn, Bonde paa Dyster, testamenterede 1 Öresbol i Gaarden Skræpheim i Kraakstad til Aas Kirke paa Follo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Originaltekst: ”Ollum monnum þæim sæm þætta bref sea æder hæyra senda Amunder Þorgazs son [Og]munder a Þuæithom ok Jon gruti q. gudes ok sina. Mer gerom yder kunnikt at aa þrættande dagh jola a x[xx]ta1 (are) rikis wars wyrdulæghs
2 CONC  herra herra Magnusar med gudes naad Noreghs Swia ok Skane konungs warom mer j Aas kirkiu a Follo. ok hæyrdum aa att Biorn bonde a Dystum hæill att allre samuisku lysti firir os ok widergek att han hafde gefwett æyrisboll jærdar e
2 CONC r ligger j Skræppæi-mum j Krakastad sokn till Aas kirkiu j testamentum sitt ok till b/oe/na-haldz firir sik ok sina kono till æwerlegha æighu æftir sina dagha. Till sanz hær vm settom (mer) wor jnsigli firir þætta bref er gortt wa
2 CONC r dæghi ok are sæm fyr sæghir.” Kilde: Efter Orig. pergament i norske Rigsarkiv. Alle 3 Segl mangler. Nummer: 148. Bagpaa: vm /oe/yris boll j Skræppæimum j Krakastada sokn. 1. Maaske mangler kun et x, hvorved Brevets Udstedelsesaa
2 CONC r vilde blive1339.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dysthæ sokn 1381.
2 CONT
2 CONT Brev datert den 3. april 1396, Saufestad:
2 CONT
2 CONT To Mænd kundgjöre, at Asbjörg Haraldsdatter gav 1 Hæfseldebol i Gaarden Dyste i Kollebu paa Thoten til Mariæ-Kirken i Oslo for sin Sjæl og deres, som för hende eiede Gaarden. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Originalteksten: ”Þæt se ollum goþom monnum kunnikt at mith Bryniulfuer Þora(l)dzson ok Gudþormer Þordzson warom a Saufustaþum er ligger j Ringesaker sookn a annan daagh paaskæ a siunde are rikis okaars virdhulighis hærræ Erix med
2 CONC h gudz nadh Norex kunungs. hørdom a at As[bi]orgh Haralz doter kiændis ok fullæ vidergangu veite at hon heuir giuith ok afhenth hefsæ(l)debool *jerdre j sunzstegarþenom j Diustum er ligger j Kolabo a Þoontne varæ Fru kirkio j Oslo
2 CONC  friæls ok hemolt fore huarium manne medh allum lunnendum fore sina saal ok þeiræ som þæt aate fore henne. til sanynde sætiom mith ookor insigli fore þette bref er giort var are ok deghi som fyrri sæghir.” Efter Orig. pergament i 
2 CONC Dipl. Arn. Magn. fasc. 80. No. 6. Seglene mangler.Nummer: 662. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Diustum (sønste), DysteS, 1447. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Diiste, 1578. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dyste, 1592. 1604. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dydsted, 1669. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dyste 1723, Dystar (eller Dystir?).
2 CONT
2 CONT Navnene kunne forklares af dust n. (nu i Folkesproget Hunkjønsord), Støv. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources/kilder:
2 CONT
2 CONT -Totens Bygdebok, bind IV: Totenvika, Folk og liv i hus, gard og grend, av Svein-Erik Ødegaard, utgitt av Toten Museum, Bøverbru 1984. Gnr. 5, Frøkenstad side 82.
2 CONT
